canvas 460 340
label "The vocabulary asc: has twelve classes, each a subclass of a W3C term. Bundle, Cluster and Concept (highlighted: the class of most items) extend SKOS, and Lesson is a kind of Concept; Procedure, Gate and Harness are PROV-O plans; Episode, Proposal and Review are PROV-O activities; Source and Attachment are PROV-O entities. A Concept points to its Sources, its Attachments and its Reviews, and items point to items through typed properties such as uses, implements, decides, verifies, covers, blocks and mentions"
caption "The highlighted class is the one most items take. Every class extends a SKOS or PROV-O term, so a reader that knows only those vocabularies can still read the graph."
region skos 10 26 136 274 "SKOS"
box bundle 20 40 116 44 "Bundle|ConceptScheme"
box cluster 20 98 116 44 "Cluster|Collection"
box concept 20 162 116 44 "Concept|skos:Concept" acc
box lesson 20 240 116 44 "Lesson"
region plan 162 26 136 150 "PROV-O plans"
box procedure 172 38 116 34 "Procedure"
box gate 172 84 116 34 "Gate"
box harness 172 130 116 34 "Harness"
region activity 314 26 136 150 "PROV-O activities"
box episode 324 38 116 34 "Episode"
box proposal 324 84 116 34 "Proposal"
box review 324 130 116 34 "Review"
region entity 162 222 288 78 "PROV-O entities"
box source 172 244 124 34 "Source"
box attachment 316 244 124 34 "Attachment"
arrow lesson concept
arrow concept review via=382,196
arrow concept source
arrow concept attachment via=152,226;152,292;378,292
note "items link to items: uses, implements, decides, verifies, blocks"
